A||N||15||grinthock||I hate my life - Failed Michigan Trip||||1||
Z||000000||grinthock||07-14-2001||07:29 AM||||Here it goes guys......<P>I couldn't take my car, had some quirky issues that bothered me... So I decided to shotgun with AkursedX (Joe).....<P>He picked me up at 7:30AM EST and we headed off to meet some of our convoy.. Met up with 5 fieros, and headed out.<P>Met up with more to bring our convoy up to 15 fieros.<P>One person had a minor clutch master leak, no issue there.<P>We got on the road made it to Sarnia Ontario and headed over the bridge.... Once in Port Huron MI we head a strange tappet noise.<P>We figured it was something in the top end, my feeling?  Stickey lifter, or a rocker issue.  Joe was running 5W30 Synthetic in his car, my mind (and apparantly everyone else who was with us, including a qualified mech) is that it was WAY too light for the driving speed and heat outside.  We stopped for gas, and the crew went on ahead and said call the hotel if there was a problem.<P>We stopped and got a Oil change 20W50 to try to fix the problem, but after 45 minutes of idling and slight revving the problem had only SLIGHTLY gone away.  Joe not wanting to risk his car decided he wanted to take it to Detroit to his uncles place (he is from Buffalo and didn't think he could make it back).  I said we could probably make it to Frankenmuth and back as the problem was ALMOST gone, Worst case is we are forced to remove the intake plenum and disable the affected cylinder (88GT).  <P>So I figured if I could find ANOTHER way back to Burlington, ON, Canada I could goto the show and just hitch a ride back.  I left 5 emergency messages for other people in our group that I knew at the hotel.  I told them it was an emergency she said she would ensure their delivery.  I called and called and nobody had arrived, and no call.  Finally, it was late, almost 5, I called again to find out that everyone had checked in and the girl had personally delivered my messages.  I received no call.<P>I decided I now needed to get home, no buses/trains from the area left till the next day and I had no interest in sitting around.  We headed to Detriot (50 miles) on the way the problem was pretty much gone, but joe didn't wanna risk driving home.  I found out before our drive to detroiot that there was a GreyHounder leaving at 1am for Ontario (close to Burlington) so I decided to take it.  I went and bought my ticket when we got to Detriot, then we went for some dinner and what not.  Then we drove to the bus station in his uncles car at 1am for the bus, Detriot is GROSS that's all I can say and at 1am I was scared out of my mind.<P>I get on the bus and things are ok, except this child was screaming the whole way, after about an hour the kid dosed off and the lady WAKES THE KID UP to see some landmark in the DARK that you can't see cause the windows are smoked anyway!! The kid starts WAILING AGAIN!!! another hour later same situtation she tries ot wake her kid, I got up and YELLED AT HER "Lady let your kid sleep so the rest of us can you stupid Bi***"<P>She responded "Don't you tell me what to do you little **** "<P>Someone else on the bus said "He speaks for all of us you stupid bi*** now shut the hell up!"<P>The kid wailed all the way home (4 hour bus ride) <P>So now I am posting this just as I goto bed here in Canada from a failed trip.<P>I am never going to a Fiero show that is more than 100klms away again.  Not worth it.  It's situations like this that make people question OWNING a Fiero.  I still love and want mine, but The whole time all we could do is be pissed.... I will post pics soon....||||reg||1
Z||000001||grinthock||07-14-2001||07:47 AM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joefinger.JPG">  <P>This is after the long day and we were almost FLAT out of options to make it to Frankenmuth... Joe is giving the finger to his BEAUTIFUL 88GT<P>The pics below are what I actually got, I planed on having hundreds.<P>More pics are located at:<BR> <A HREF="http://grinthock.2y.net/failedtrip/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://grinthock.2y.net/failedtrip/index.html</A> <p>[This message has been edited by grinthock (edited 07-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||banditbalz||07-14-2001||08:07 AM||||sorry to hear about the rotten trip down Grinthock. The pics look great. Seems everyone was displaying their middle finger. ha haa<BR>I guess the Burlington boys have some explaining to do when they get back home.<BR>At least we have the Toronto show to look forward too.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Untitled_2.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||12
Z||000003||Formula88||07-14-2001||11:47 AM||||Must have been Friday the 13th.  Getting ready for a trip to the beach with a bunch of Fiero friends, Bob's car develops a sudden crack in the exhaust manifold, and he's out.  Then I go outside to pack my Formula and find a big screw stuck in my front tire.  I think it can be fixed, but I didn't want to test it with a 400+ mile test drive.  So, I'm at home today instead of being at the beach, where I belong!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000004||grinthock||07-14-2001||03:04 PM||||Yeah I thought about the date too... Oh well.  I just hope someone takes as many pics as I planned, I was going to take over 500 pics and put them on a CD for everyone||||reg||1
Z||000005||AkursedX||07-14-2001||08:55 PM||||Well, I'm home now.  <P>I'm glad you made it home Grinthock, although you should of beat the crap out of the kid  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Well, my dad showed up late in the morning, and we went out and got breakfast and spent some time with my Uncle.  I started the car up again and it was ticking really loud again but quieted down real quick.  Then we put some of that marvel mystery oil in the pan, and after a little bit of driving, the problem was just about non-exsistant.  So kudos to marvel mystery oil.  The stuff works good.  But it didn't fix my problem completely.  <P>So anyways.  I drove home at around 60-65mph and didn't have any problems.  Thank GOD! But the long drive took it's toll.  It doesn't really sound good at all.  <P>So, tomorrow starts my project.  I'm getting a little bit of money soon, so I will have the cash for parts.  I plan on replacing the lifters, pushrods, and rocker arms with hi-po parts.  And hopefully, my problem will be cured.  And maybe I'll have a little more power.<P>Then, I decide if I am going to sell it.<P>Right now I am not really mad at my car.  Things like this are expected. But, with this whole ordeal, and the fact that it left me stranded a week ago with a bad coil, and other little quirks and fixes within the past 2 weeks, I am just sick and tired of it.   But, we'll see.  I'm just really turned off to Fieros right now.<P>On a positive note.  I made the trip from Buffalo to detroit in less than a tank of gas.  I average about 26 miles to a gallon in an auto.  That's pretty impressive as far as I see it.  <P>Well, I think I am hoing to go and start the tear-down process.  <BR><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||AkursedX||07-14-2001||11:00 PM||||Oh yeah, George, I'll get your cover and stuff back to you as soon as I can.  And didn't I take that picture of your car??  Did you get it from PIP??  Just curious.  <P>Well, time to go out and get drunk.  I really need it right now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
